From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liam Brady <lbrady@google.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 16:06:48 -0700
Subject: Restore original URL for resource timing and observers

This CL restores the unsanitized original URL in the browser-side
ResourceLoadComplete and in the renderer-side iframe ResourceTiming.

When URL sanitization is enabled, the renderer only receives an
origin-only version of the original URL for cross-origin navigations. To
ensure features like Resource Timing continue to function correctly,
this change:

- Stores the full original URL in DocumentAssociatedData at commit time.
- Restores the unsanitized URL in the browser process before notifying
  observers.
- Updates the ResourceLoadComplete observer to pass this
  browser-provided original URL explicitly.
- Restores the unsanitized URL for iframe subresource timing in Blink
  using fallback timing information. This is information the embedder's
  renderer already has access to.
- Removes an early return in `HTMLFrameOwnerElement::AddResourceTiming`.
  The bug mentioned in the comment is marked as closed, and the name
  check is no longer necessary.

